  <h2>TL;DR: readiness comes before more demand</h2>
  <p class="answer-first">
    Get New Patients is an acquisition-system decision, not a promise of a particular lead, booking,
    patient, or revenue result. A practice is better prepared when it has service capacity, an
    approved offer, a realistic budget, a tested inquiry path, and named owners for response and
    measurement. If one of those is missing, fix the handoff before increasing traffic.
  </p>

  <h2>Is your practice ready to add demand?</h2>
  <p>
    Start with the operating constraint. A campaign can create attention or inquiries, but it cannot
    open clinical capacity, approve an offer, answer an exception, or confirm that a person attended.
    Use this readiness check before selecting a channel.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Capacity:</strong> document open appointment capacity by location and appointment type.</li>
    <li><strong>Offer:</strong> approve the service facts, eligibility, price language, and claims that may appear publicly.</li>
    <li><strong>Budget:</strong> separate the media budget from service fees and choose a decision window in the written plan.</li>
    <li><strong>Destination:</strong> test the landing page, form, phone, calendar, and confirmation path that a prospect will use.</li>
    <li><strong>Response:</strong> name the owner for first contact, exceptions, confirmation, rescheduling, and missed appointments.</li>
    <li><strong>Measurement:</strong> define each stage and identify the system that proves it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If your main constraint is choosing among services, start with the
    <a href="/services/">ChiroCandy services decision guide</a>. If your team needs a broader plan,
    use the
    <a href="/blog/a-comprehensive-marketing-plan-for-chiropractors/">
      chiropractic marketing plan
    </a>
    to assign owners and decision dates first.
  </p>

  <h2>What can the acquisition system include?</h2>
  <p class="answer-first">
    The channel mix and handoff should match the signed proposal. Do not assume that every ad
    platform, landing page, automation, calendar, payment tool, SEO service, or reactivation workflow
    is included in every engagement.
  </p>
  <p>
    A proposed system may combine
    <a href="/services/facebook-advertising/">Facebook and Instagram advertising</a>,
    <a href="/services/google-advertising/">Google Ads</a>, a landing or booking destination, and an
    agreed response workflow. The scope should identify the accounts, creative, software, media
    budget, approvals, practice inputs, exclusions, launch acceptance checks, and reporting fields.
    Use the <a href="/pricing/">marketing cost guide</a> and
    <a href="/marketing-calculator/">marketing calculator</a> to prepare the budget conversation;
    they are planning tools, not outcome forecasts.
  </p>

  <h2>How should the lead handoff work?</h2>
  <p>
    Draw the handoff from the first platform result to the practice's final business record. Assign
    one source of truth and one owner to each stage:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Platform result:</strong> the result reported by the advertising platform under its selected objective.</li>
    <li><strong>Unique inquiry:</strong> a deduplicated person who contacted the practice.</li>
    <li><strong>Qualified inquiry:</strong> a person who meets the practice's documented, non-clinical intake criteria.</li>
    <li><strong>Appointment request:</strong> a requested time or next step that still may need confirmation.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirmed booking:</strong> an appointment accepted in the practice's scheduling record.</li>
    <li><strong>Held visit:</strong> a confirmed booking that the practice records as attended.</li>
    <li><strong>Patient and revenue records:</strong> practice-side outcomes reconciled in the appropriate business system.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Google explains that an Analytics key event is a configured event that the business marks as
    important. That makes its meaning dependent on the event and setup; it does not automatically
    establish a confirmed booking, held visit, patient, or revenue. See
    <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/9267568">Google Analytics' key-event documentation</a>.
    The
    <a href="/blog/chiropractic-advertising-leads-to-appointments/">lead-to-appointment handoff guide</a>
    shows how to reconcile the stages without converting a lead count into a patient claim.
  </p>

  <h2>Who owns each part of the workflow?</h2>
  <p>
    Put the owner and backup in the launch document. ChiroCandy can manage the marketing work listed
    in the proposal. The practice supplies approved facts, timely access and approvals, response
    coverage, scheduling decisions, care decisions, and downstream records. Any automation should
    have an escalation path for questions or situations it is not approved to handle.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>ChiroCandy:</strong> complete the agreed campaign, creative, destination, and reporting work.</li>
    <li><strong>Practice:</strong> approve public claims, maintain capacity, handle exceptions, confirm appointments, and record attendance.</li>
    <li><strong>Shared:</strong> test the handoff, agree on definitions, review discrepancies, and decide whether to continue, revise, pause, or expand.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What does documented campaign evidence show?</h2>
  <p>
    The
    <a href="/case-studies/lifeworks-family-chiropractic-kelowna/">LifeWorks Family Chiropractic case study</a>
    publishes a Meta report covering June 2 through August 31, 2026. The two lead campaigns recorded
    185 platform lead results on $2,734.59 in spend, a calculated $14.78 per reported lead result.
    The case explicitly does not establish unique people, workshop attendance, booked appointments,
    held visits, or patient acquisition cost. It is useful evidence for the platform stage—not a
    forecast for another practice or proof of downstream outcomes.
  </p>

  <h2>When is Get New Patients a fit?</h2>
  <p class="answer-first">
    It may fit an established practice that can accept more demand, has an offer ready for public
    use, can fund the agreed plan, and will own the response and measurement handoff. It is not ready
    to scale when those foundations are missing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choose <a href="/done-for-you-program/">Done-For-You</a> when you want ChiroCandy to manage the
    agreed marketing execution. Choose the <a href="/training-program/">Training Program</a> when an
    internal owner will learn and execute the playbooks. Get New Patients is the acquisition-system
    question that either delivery model can support; the proposal defines what is actually included.
  </p>
  <p>
    To prepare for a discovery call, bring your weekly capacity, approved offer, current response
    owner, booking workflow, proposed media budget, and the stages your practice can verify. The call
    should determine fit and next steps—not promise a result before the operating facts are known.
  </p>
